segment.source:
::Scars left by the lightning strike leave a remarkable shape colored in red, featuring a pattern closely resembling plant roots. On several spots, these wounds rupture the body, further revealing the devastating damage caused by the impact. 

From time to time, the physician would gently touch the corpse with his left hand in search for signs of life. As he moves from one spot to another, the mild mist of dust perfectly makes way so that it wouldn't make contact with him.::

Malformations... colors of doubt... stench of foul regret... a pulsating weight of any temperature... I must find it all... and cleanse it. Only then the transformation is complete.&lt;end&gt;

